Build a coherent mine-to-product study across extraction, processing, operation, and closure (@mine-integrated-project: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mining-and-mineral-engineering, #source "../sources/Hard-Rock-Miners-Handbook.lingua#r_18YBY5XX4TFS7ZQSKTQMW34EFA", #source "../sources/CETEM-Usinas-de-Beneficiamento.lingua#r_62ZD994C9YYXB1YDVFQST5B27J", #source "../sources/Resource-and-Reserve-Reporting-CRIRSCO-CBRR.lingua#r_2CZZ64T1W8VC542VCNCH2E6DSR", #source "../sources/SME-Mining-Engineering-Handbook.lingua#r_4Y1TJWVHWWCYTYAKZKMAEAVX25", #source "../sources/Mine-Closure-Leading-Practice.lingua#r_2GYS4C9MHF2CRD8253QPDEV3QN", #mining-and-mineral-engineering "Independent-mining-and-mineral-engineering-scholarship.lingua#r_6W8ZNWYXBYCFRMSPEVT5AVSWV8") { r_1WXCC9JS4RM4E27NGJC8ZXYE5B
**Read:** [Hard Rock Miner’s Handbook — Jack de la Vergne, fifth edition](../sources/Hard-Rock-Miners-Handbook.lingua#r_18YBY5XX4TFS7ZQSKTQMW34EFA), the whole handbook revisited for connected systems; [Usinas de Beneficiamento de Minérios do Brasil — CETEM](../sources/CETEM-Usinas-de-Beneficiamento.lingua#r_62ZD994C9YYXB1YDVFQST5B27J), complete integrated and comparison cases; [Resources, reserves, and technical-study definitions — CRIRSCO and CBRR](../sources/Resource-and-Reserve-Reporting-CRIRSCO-CBRR.lingua#r_2CZZ64T1W8VC542VCNCH2E6DSR), the full technical-study definitions and evidence context; [SME Mining Engineering Handbook — Peter Darling, third edition](../sources/SME-Mining-Engineering-Handbook.lingua#r_4Y1TJWVHWWCYTYAKZKMAEAVX25), whole relevant professional chapters, when available; [Mine closure — Australian leading-practice handbook](../sources/Mine-Closure-Leading-Practice.lingua#r_2GYS4C9MHF2CRD8253QPDEV3QN), the complete closure account.

Choose a material need and one documented deposit-to-product system. Combine the geological/resource evidence, method/layout, ground/sequence, equipment/transport, ventilation/water/power, processing, product/custody, workers, supplies, waste, closure, and post-closure work into one coherent technical account. Reuse the preceding studies and shared foundations rather than silently changing their assumptions at each interface.

Develop a baseline and at least two substantive alternatives. Preserve all material/constituent/water balances, energy bases, timescales, capacity/availability assumptions, quality distributions, and uncertainty. Check that the mine feed actually supplies the modeled plant, the services support the proposed sequence, and the final usable product has the claimed specification and custody evidence.

Test adverse feed, a consequential equipment/utility interruption, and early closure. Follow changes across system boundaries rather than holding every downstream operation ideal. Examine consequences for affected people, work, maintenance, restoration, waste, and future use. Explain whether a reported improvement reduces total connected work or moves it elsewhere.

**Work:** deliver a substantial design/operation/recovery study with primary bibliography, derivations, inspectable calculations, independent checks, observations, alternatives, and defended conclusions. Have an independent reader reproduce a core result and challenge the weakest consequential assumption. Revise the study from evidence and retain disagreements. Explicitly separate literature/software conclusions from laboratory, field, and operating competence actually demonstrated. The next scholarship step asks a new research question rather than treating this integrated account as the end of the subject.

**Continue:** [Investigate an unresolved mining or mineral-processing question with independent evidence](Independent-mining-and-mineral-engineering-scholarship.lingua#r_6W8ZNWYXBYCFRMSPEVT5AVSWV8).

**Return:** [Mining and mineral engineering — extraction, processing, and continuing work](../Mining-and-mineral-engineering.lingua#r_22HJPS3RTK5EX1J55YJP75PHYA).
